  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "In the {past}few years, {online}learning has become a {significant}part of the {university}and college experience.A {survey}found that 29 percent of college students {register}for online courses.But are all online courses created {equal}? How can you be sure that digital learning is {right}for you? If you take an online course, what can you do to ensure the best {possible}grade?",
      "cn": "在 <u> 过去的 </u> 几年里， <u> 在线 </u> 学习已经成为 <u> 大学 </u> 和学院生活的 <u> 重要 </u> 组成部分。一项 <u> 调查 </u> 发现，29%的大学生 <u> 注册 </u> 了在线课程。但是所有在线课程都 <u> 一样 </u> 吗？你如何确定数字化学习 <u> 适合 </u> 你呢？如果你选择了一门在线课程，你能做些什么来确保尽 <u> 可能 </u> 好的成绩呢？"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "We {interview}students and professors to get their {advice}about online courses.The most {obvious} {advantage} of online learning is that you can study {anywhere}and {anytime}.But that doesn't mean there aren't {deadline}.“I think a point that many people {lose} {sight} of is how easy it can be to {fall}behind schedule,”says {graduate}student Amanda Bindman.Before choosing to study online, consider whether you're a self-motivated learner and if the {material}seems {interesting}enough to {keep}you going.",
      "cn": "我们 <u> 采访 </u> 了学生和教授们，以了解他们对在线课程的 <u> 建议 </u> 。在线学习最 <u> 明显的优势 </u> 在于你可以 <u> 随时随地 </u> 学习，但这并不意味着没有 <u> 截止日期 </u> 。 <u> 研究生 </u> 阿曼达·宾德曼说：“我认为很多人都 <u> 忽略 </u> 了一点，那就是学习进度很容易 <u> 落 </u> 后。”在选择在线学习之前，请想想你是否是一个自主学习者，以及学习 <u> 材料 </u> 看起来是否足够 <u> 有趣 </u> ，能 <u> 使 </u> 你 <u> 坚持 </u> 学下去。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "The tip that comes up most often is {simple}: build online courses into your {weekly}schedule, just like what you would do with in-person courses.Professor Alex Davidson teaches the same course in person and online.He noted that his online students usually {end}up with lower grades.It is so easy to let an online course {slide}, but your grades will {suffer}as a result.Be sure to schedule set times to watch your lectures, read materials and {contribute}to online {discussion} {board} .",
      "cn": "最常被提及的建议很 <u> 简单 </u> ：将在线课程纳入你 <u> 每周的 </u> 日程中，就像你在面授课程中所做的那样。亚历克斯·戴维森教授同时教线下和线上课程。他指出，自己线上课程的学生 <u> 最后 </u> 的成绩通常较差。 <u> 放任 </u> 一门在线课程 <u> 不管 </u> 是很容易的，但结果是你的成绩会 <u> 退步 </u> 。一定要安排固定的时间来观看课程视频、阅读相关资料以及 <u> 参与 </u> 线上 <u> 讨论区 </u> 的交流。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "The {chief} {complaint} about online courses is that they {lack}human {interaction}.A social {connection}is often a big part of learning.There are things you can do to {ease}this {problem}.Jessica Pink, an {undergraduate}student, {suggest}taking online courses with a {friend}, so you can {motivate}each other to stay on {track}.You can also find students on the class discussion board to {organize}a study group, or schedule in-person {meeting}with your professor to discuss course concepts.",
      "cn": "人们对在线课程的 <u> 主要抱怨 </u> 是其 <u> 缺乏 </u> 人际 <u> 互动 </u> 。社交 <u> 联系 </u> 往往是学习中的一个重要组成部分。你可以做一些事情来 <u> 缓解 </u> 这个 <u> 问题 </u> 。 <u> 本科生 </u> 杰西卡·平克 <u> 建议 </u> 与 <u> 朋友 </u> 一起参加在线课程，这样可以互相 <u> 激励 </u> ，保持学习 <u> 进度 </u> 。你还可以在课堂讨论区找到学生 <u> 组织 </u> 一个学习小组，或安排与教授面对面的 <u> 会议 </u> 来讨论课程概念。"
    }
  ],
